        text="C130237",
        description="""\"Stage IB includes: T2, N0, M0, B0-1. T2: Patches, papules, or plaques covering 10% or more of the skin surface.  May further stratify into T2a (patch only) vs. T2b (plaque +/- patch).  N0: No clinically abnormal peripheral lymph nodes; biopsy not required.  M0: No visceral organ involvement.  B0: Absence of significant blood involvement: 5% or less of peripheral blood lymphocytes are atypical (Sezary cells).  B1: Low blood tumor burden: more than 5% of peripheral blood lymphocytes are atypi...""",
