        description="""\"A rare inherited form of myofibromatosis caused by autosomal dominant mutation(s) in the PDGFRB gene, encoding platelet-derived growth factor receptor beta. The condition is characterized by the onset of solitary or multicentric benign tumors in the skin, striated muscles, bones, and viscera. The lesions may be present at birth or become apparent in early infancy or even occasionally in adult life.\"""",
