        description="""\"An autosomal recessive subtype of Parkinson disease, caused by mutation(s) in the DNAJC6 gene, encoding putative tyrosine-protein phosphatase auxilin. It is characterized by an onset of Parkinsonism between the third and fifth decades. Mutations(s) in DNAJC6, are also causative in PARK19A.\"""",
